<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s191S"><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s191w1">gsum pa</span> de dag <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s191p1">gi</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s191w2">&#x27;bras bu</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s191p2">la</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s191w3">gsum</span> las, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s191w4">rnam smin</span> <span class="u case" data-d="6" data-l="s191p3">gyi</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s191w5">&#x27;bras bu</span> <span class="u topic" data-d="6" data-l="s191p4">ni</span></span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s191S">Here is the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s191w1">third</span> section, a presentation <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s191p2">on</span> the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s191w2">consequences</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s191p1">of</span> the various kinds of bad deeds. We proceed in <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s191w3">three</span> parts, beginning with what are called the &quot;<span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s191w4">ripened</span>&quot; <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s191w5">consequences</span>.<span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s191p3"><span class="nul">Genitive relation expressed by English attributive ripened; no separate word.</span></span><span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s191p4"><span class="nul">Topic marking has no separate English exponent.</span></span></span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; Codex reconciliation; PROVISIONAL machine alignment. de dag is expanded anaphorically as the various kinds of bad deeds and is omitted as distributed reference. gi owns of; la marks the consequences as the domain of the division and is rendered on in the recast presentation. gyi has no separately alignable exponent because its genitive relation is fused into English attributive ripened; ni has no distinct word apart from the topic framing. third and three exclude explanatory section and parts. las and beginning with what are called participate in enumerative restructuring and are left unpaired.</div>
